    "explanation": "The lifecycle is tracked with current time, phase, job ID, attempt, and deadline. A start is accepted unless work is pending or waiting. Fail and success affect state only for the matching pending job and attempt. A retry failure enters waiting with a deadline based on the larger of configured delay and the supplied minimum delay. Advance moves time and promotes at most one due retry. Terminal jobs can be started again; irrelevant responses are ignored.",
    "program": "function solve(x){var c=x.config,e=x.event,s=x.state;if(s==null)s={now:0,phase:'idle',id:null,attempt:0,due:null};else s={now:s.now,phase:s.phase,id:s.id,attempt:s.attempt,due:s.due};var send=[],status='ignored',t=e.type;if(t==='start'){if(s.phase==='pending'||s.phase==='waiting')status='busy';else{s.id=e.id;s.attempt=1;s.phase='pending';s.due=null;send=[{id:s.id,attempt:1}];status='started'}}else if(t==='fail'){if(s.phase==='pending'&&s.id===e.id&&s.attempt===e.attempt){if(s.attempt>=c.attempts){s.phase='failed';s.due=null;status='failed'}else{s.phase='waiting';s.due=s.now+Math.max(c.delay,e.after);status='waiting'}}}else if(t==='success'){if(s.phase==='pending'&&s.id===e.id&&s.attempt===e.attempt){s.phase='succeeded';s.due=null;status='succeeded'}}else if(t==='cancel'){if(s.phase==='pending'||s.phase==='waiting'){s.phase='cancelled';s.due=null;status='cancelled'}}else if(t==='advance'){s.now+=e.dt;if(s.phase==='waiting'&&s.now>=s.due){s.attempt++;s.phase='pending';s.due=null;send=[{id:s.id,attempt:s.attempt}]}status='advanced'}return{state:s,output:{status:status,phase:s.phase,id:s.id,attempt:s.attempt,due:s.due,now:s.now,send:send}}}"
